Note that, while ''mizu'' is the most general Japanese term for “{{m-lite|en|water}}”, it does refer specifically to “{{m|en|[[water]] that is not [[hot]]}}”.  Meanwhile, the word {{m-lite|ja|sc=Jpan|湯|tr=yu}} refers specifically to “{{m-lite|en|hot water}}”.  Consider {{m-lite|ja|sc=Jpan|水風呂||tr=mizu-buro|[[cold]]-[[water]] [[bath]]}}, contrasting with {{m-lite|ja|sc=Jpan|風呂||tr=furo|pos=implying hot water|[[bath]]}}.

